      "id": 1,
      "text": "Dorris was named for Presley Dorris of the D Ranch and became incorporated on December 21, 1908.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.dorrisca.us/about/"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Southern Pacific Railroad’s arrival in the northern Butte Valley sparked the founding of the city of Dorris.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.dorrisca.us/about/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Dorris sits in the Butte Valley, 41°57′54″N 121°55′8″W, between Mount Shasta and the Oregon border.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10,
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dorris%2C_California"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The town’s Little League Complex, library, and New Centennial History/Sculpture Wall showcase the community’s volunteer spirit.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.dorrisca.us/about/"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Dorris’s flagpole and county library are the only listed attractions, reflecting the town’s modest but proud heritage.",
